## System Architecture Diagram (to include in `Architecture/MOT_System_Architecture.md`)

```mermaid
flowchart TB
    subgraph Jetson["Jetson Nano — Main Processor"]
        FE["Frontend<br/>(HTML/CSS/JS)"]
        BE["Backend<br/>(Python / Flask)"]
        FE <--> BE
    end

    subgraph MainPCB["Main PCB — STM32F407VGTx"]
        BL["Bootloader<br/>(Sector 0)"]
        APP["FreeRTOS App<br/>(Bank A / B)"]
    end

    subgraph STM8_Sensors["STM8 Sensor Boards"]
        PS["Pressure Sensor Board<br/>STM8 + ELVH-F50D"]
        TH["Temp/Humidity Board<br/>STM8 + SHT40"]
    end

    subgraph Display["Surgeon Display — STM32"]
        SD["STM32 + LCD"]
    end

    subgraph RGB["RGB LED Controllers — ESP32"]
        RS["RGB Modbus Slave"]
        RT["RGB TCP Slave"]
        RD["RGB DMX Slave"]
    end

    subgraph XRAY["X-Ray Viewer — STM8"]
        XV["STM8 + Relay"]
    end

    BE -- "UART (GPIO 8 TX, 10 RX)" --> APP
    BE -- "UART5 (OTA)" --> BL
    BE -- "USB → RS-485 Converter" --> SD
    BE -- "USB → RS-485 Converter" --> RS
    BE -- "WiFi (TCP)" --> RT
    BE -- "DMX" --> RD

    PS -- "I2C → PWM out" --> MainPCB
    TH -- "I2C → PWM out" --> MainPCB
    APP -- "ADC reads PWM" --> STM8_Sensors
```

### Wiring & Converters Between STM8 and STM32

The STM8 sensor boards do **not** use a direct digital protocol (UART / SPI) to send data to the STM32. Instead:

```
┌───────────────────────┐     PWM Signal     ┌──────────────────────────────┐
│  STM8 Sensor Board    │ ──────────────────► │  STM32 Main PCB              │
│                       │   (0–100% duty)     │                              │
│  Sensor ──I2C──► MCU  │                     │  ADC Pin ◄── RC Low-Pass     │
│           ↓           │                     │  Filter smooths PWM to       │
│  MCU generates PWM    │                     │  analog voltage              │
│  proportional to      │                     │                              │
│  sensor reading       │                     │  ADC converts to digital     │
└───────────────────────┘                     └──────────────────────────────┘
```

| Connection | From | To | Method | Converter / IC |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Sensor → STM8 | ELVH-F50D / SHT40 | STM8 I2C pins | I2C bus | 4.7 kΩ pull-ups |
| STM8 → STM32 | STM8 PWM output pin | STM32 ADC input pin | PWM → Analog | RC low-pass filter (R + C) |
| Jetson → STM32 | Jetson GPIO 8/10 | STM32 UART RX/TX | UART (3.3 V) | Direct or level shifter |
| Jetson → STM32 (OTA) | Jetson UART | STM32 UART5 | UART (9600 baud) | Direct |
| Jetson → Surgeon Disp | Jetson USB | STM32 UART | RS-485 | USB-to-RS-485 dongle (e.g. CH340 + MAX485) |
| Jetson → RGB Slaves | Jetson USB | ESP32 UART | RS-485 Modbus | USB-to-RS-485 dongle |
| Jetson → RGB TCP | WiFi | ESP32 WiFi | TCP socket | No hardware converter |

---

## Learning Order

We learn firmware in dependency order (lowest-level first):

| # | Firmware | MCU | Controller Doc First? | Protocols Touched |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | **MOT-ELVH-STM8** (pressure sensor) | STM8S003F3P | Yes → `Controllers/STM8.md` | I2C, PWM, UART |
| 2 | **MOT-SHT40-STM8** (temp/humidity) | STM8S003F3P | No (already done) | I2C, PWM, UART |
| 3 | **MOT-CONTROLLER-CARD** (main PCB) | STM32F407VGTx | Yes → `Controllers/STM32.md` | UART, ADC, PWM |
| 4 | **MOT-STM32-BOOTLOADER** | STM32F407VGTx | No (already done) | UART, OTA Protocol |
| 5 | **MOT-SURGEON-DISP** | STM32 | No | UART, RS-485 |
| 6 | **MOT-RGB-SLAVE** (Modbus) | ESP32 | Yes → `Controllers/ESP32.md` | Modbus, RS-485 |
| 7 | **MOT-RGB-TCP** | ESP32 | No | TCP, WiFi |
| 8 | **MOT-RGB-DMX** | ESP32 | No | DMX |
| 9 | **XRAY-VIEWER-STM8** | STM8 | No | GPIO, Relay |

---

## Document Style Guidelines

Based on the user's preferred styles:

1. **Flash Memory Layout style** — Use ASCII tables with sector addresses, sizes, and assignments (as in [MOT-STM32-BOOTLOADER/README.md](file:///c:/Users/oml/Documents/BitBucket/MOT/MOT-STM32-BOOTLOADER/README.md))
2. **Byte-Level Conversation style** — Show actual hex bytes on the wire with annotations (as in Conversation Example section)
3. **Mermaid diagrams** — Use `flowchart TD/LR` for flow diagrams, data paths, and architecture overviews (as in `walkthrough.md`)
4. **Step-by-step tables** — Use time-based tables showing events and internal state (as in CommandThrottle walkthrough)
5. **Register bit diagrams** — Use ASCII box-drawing for 8/16/32-bit register layouts
6. **Code with inline comments** — Show actual firmware code with detailed `// ←` annotations

### Document Naming Convention

| Type | Pattern | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Firmware guide | `Firmware/<REPO>/FIRMWARE_GUIDE.md` | `Firmware/MOT-ELVH-STM8/FIRMWARE_GUIDE.md` |
| Controller ref | `Controllers/<MCU>.md` | `Controllers/STM8.md` |
| Protocol ref | `Protocols/<PROTOCOL>.md` | `Protocols/I2C.md` |
| Fundamentals | `Fundamentals/<TOPIC>.md` | `Fundamentals/PWM.md` |
| Architecture | `Architecture/MOT_System_Architecture.md` | — |

---

## Proposed Changes

### [NEW] Docs/README.md
Master index and learning roadmap. Links to all documents, shows recommended learning order, tracks completion.

### [NEW] Architecture/MOT_System_Architecture.md
Full system overview with mermaid diagram, wiring table, converter details, and data-flow explanations.

### [NEW] Firmware/ folder structure
Empty `FIRMWARE_GUIDE.md` placeholder for each repo (to be filled as we learn each firmware).

### [NEW] Controllers/ folder
- `STM8.md` — Created **before** we start learning MOT-ELVH-STM8
- `STM32.md` — Created **before** we start learning MOT-CONTROLLER-CARD
- `ESP32.md` — Created **before** we start learning MOT-RGB-SLAVE

### [NEW] Protocols/ folder
One file per protocol, created on demand as firmware learning encounters them.

### [NEW] Fundamentals/ folder
Topic documents created on demand. `PWM.md` will be extensive; smaller topics like reserved registers go into `Memory_and_Registers.md`.

